      ],
      "title": "CMake: Add guards for PLATFORM sanity check",
      "message": "CMake: Add guards for PLATFORM sanity check\n\nThe sanity check is specific for Visual Studio so add those\nguards. The PLATFORM variable is not standard for other toolchains.\n\nAdd a default \"windows target platform\" of Win64.\n\nAdd error output for win-setup.ps1.\n",
      "author_name": "João Valverde",
      "author_email": "j@v6e.pt",
      "authored_date": "2021-09-20T14:14:03.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "João Valverde",
      "committer_email": "j@v6e.pt",
      "committed_date": "2021-09-20T15:11:52.000+01:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/bb12a187df01c3789fae3c1a1d07e3bf9837e5e1"
    },
    {
      "id": "8726c652674a5f8f8e2d45abc7205b9ad054f69f",
      "short_id": "8726c652",
      "created_at": "2021-09-20T14:38:03.000+01:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "c513188f52bc2f66e7700bab2e870f17ac973646"
      ],
      "title": "win-setup.ps1: Be more lax about validating path separators",
      "message": "win-setup.ps1: Be more lax about validating path separators\n\nCMake file(TO_NATIVE_PATH) doesn't do the right thing on MinGW[1],\nbut Windows supports backslash and forward slash.\n\n[1]https://gitlab.kitware.com/cmake/cmake/-/issues/5939\n",
      "author_name": "João Valverde",
      "author_email": "j@v6e.pt",
      "authored_date": "2021-09-20T14:34:01.000+01:00",
